SUMMARY:Deadline: Art Worker Artist Grant 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Art Worker Artist Grant is a biennial award for artists who
 se livelihoods are connected to the production\, handling\, exhibition\, c
 are\, movement or stewardship of art. Its premise is that a great many art
 ists fund their practice through labour inside the art industry itself\, a
 nd that this work rarely comes with support for their own artistic develop
 ment. WHO IS ELIGIBLE: artists who support their practice by providing any
  form of labour in any area of the art industry\, including but not limite
 d to museums\, galleries\, artist studios\, collections\, auction houses\,
  art fairs\, fabrication\, framing and mountmaking workshops\, conservatio
 n labs\, art logistics and crating companies\, and storage facilities. WHA
 T IT FUNDS: the development of artistic work in whatever form that takes\,
  with the money explicitly unrestricted\; the call lists studio time\, tra
 vel\, healthcare\, research\, equipment\, rest\, materials\, living expens
 es and childcare as legitimate uses. There are no required outcomes and no
  required acquittal\, so no reporting obligation. APPLICATION: intentional
 ly minimal\, consisting of a brief statement describing how the funds coul
 d support artistic development or production\, and a link to a website\, p
 ortfolio\, social media or other documentation of the work. SELECTION: by 
 an independent jury of Andria Hickey (curator and museum leader\, curatori
 al advisor for the Barclays Center art programme in Brooklyn\, previously 
 at The Shed\, Pace Gallery and MOCA Cleveland)\, Clynton Lowry (artist and
  publisher) and Paul Graham (photographer). IMPORTANT: applications for th
 e 2026 edition are capped at the first 500 submissions\, so the call may c
 lose before the stated deadline. Key dates in AEST: entries open 24 August
  2026\, entries close 14 September 2026\, recipient announced 2 November 2
 026. Overseen and funded by ARTIST ENGINEERING.\n\nOrganisation: ARTIST EN
 GINEERING\nLocation: Remote. No geographic restriction is stated in the ca
 ll\; key dates are given in AEST.\nAward: AUD 5\,000 to one recipient for 
 the 2026 edition. Funds are unrestricted: they may be used for studio time
 \, travel\, healthcare\, research\, equipment\, rest\, materials\, living 
 expenses\, childcare\, or something else entirely. There are no required o
 utcomes and no required grant acquittal. No application fee is mentioned.\
 nDuration: One-off unrestricted grant\, awarded biennially\n\nMore: https:
 //artistengineering.co/pages/awa?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm
 _medium=referral
